\newlabel{fig:prop1}{{2}{8}{Empirical verification of Proposition~1 on an engineered voting game with $p_-^i = 0.0333$ (500 trials per $K$). Theory (solid line) and empirical rates (open circles) agree closely ($r = 0.9993$). For sparse harmful contexts ($p_- \ll 1$), Algorithm~A requires $K \approx 100$ to reach 95\% detection}{figure.2}{}}
